Test file with planes of opposite signs
c
c This tests that two planes representing the same geometry
c but with negated coefficients are correctly deduplicated.
c
c In MCNP, "p a b c d" means ax + by + cz = d (not + d = 0)
c So plane at x=5:
c   px 5        -> x = 5
c   p 1 0 0 5   -> 1*x + 0*y + 0*z = 5 -> x = 5 (same plane)
c   p -1 0 0 -5 -> -x = -5 -> x = 5 (same plane, negated normal)
c
c Cell cards
c
1  0  -1 -10    $ x < 5, inside bounding sphere
2  0  -2 -10    $ x > 5 (negative sense on negated plane means x > 5)
c
99 0   10       $ graveyard

c Surface cards
c
c Plane at x=5 expressed two ways
1  px  5        $ x = 5
2  p  -1 0 0 -5 $ -x = -5, same as x = 5 but with negated normal
c
c Bounding sphere
10 so  20       $ sphere r=20

